(6133, '', '', '', ''),
(6134, '<div>\"Archives Hermès\" refers to the body of historical works and documentation of the Hermès house, and not a specific group of artists</div>\n\n<p>. Various artists and designers have contributed to Hermès\' creations over the years, and their work may be featured in \"Hermès Heritage\" exhibitions or publications that draw from these archives.<span class=\"uJ19be notranslate\"><span class=\"vKEkVd\"> </span></span></p>\n\n<div class=\"Y3BBE\"> </div>\n\n<div class=\"Y3BBE\">Key artists and individuals associated with works found within the Hermès archives include:</div>\n\n<div class=\"Y3BBE\"> </div>\n\n<ul class=\"KsbFXc U6u95\">\n	<li><span class=\"T286Pc\"><strong class=\"Yjhzub\"><span class=\"T286Pc\"><span class=\"T286Pc\">Robert Dallet</span></span></strong> A painter known for his realistic and detailed depictions of wild cats, many of which were used in Hermès scarf designs in the 1980s.</span></li>\n	<li><span class=\"T286Pc\"><strong class=\"Yjhzub\"><span class=\"T286Pc\"><span class=\"T286Pc\">Hugo Grygkar</span></span></strong><span class=\"T286Pc\"> Designer who created the renowned \"Brides de Gala\" scarf print in collaboration with <span class=\"T286Pc\">Robert Dumas</span> in 1957</span>.</span></li>\n	<li><span class=\"T286Pc\"><strong class=\"Yjhzub\"><span class=\"T286Pc\"><span class=\"T286Pc\">Leila Menchari</span></span></strong> A designer and longtime window dresser for Hermès, known for her elaborate and imaginative window displays.</span></li>\n	<li><span class=\"T286Pc\"><strong class=\"Yjhzub\"><span class=\"T286Pc\"><span class=\"T286Pc\">Daniel Aron</span></span></strong> A photographer whose images of iconic items like the Kelly bag are part of the archives.</span></li>\n	<li><span class=\"T286Pc\"><strong class=\"Yjhzub\">Draeger</strong> A name or entity (possibly a design studio or photo agency like \"Wallace et Draeger\") credited with numerous archival photographs of Hermès bags and products across several decades.</span></li>\n	<li><span class=\"T286Pc\"><strong class=\"Yjhzub\"><span class=\"T286Pc\"><span class=\"T286Pc\">Benoit Pierre Emery</span></span></strong> A French art director who created designs like the \"Échec au roi\" for scarves.</span></li>\n	<li><span class=\"T286Pc\"><strong class=\"Yjhzub\"><span class=\"T286Pc\"><span class=\"T286Pc\">Evan Hecox</span></span></strong> An American artist who created typography-based designs, such as one featuring the address \"Hermès 24 rue du Faubourg-Saint-Honoré Paris\".</span></li>\n	<li><span class=\"T286Pc\"><strong class=\"Yjhzub\"><span class=\"T286Pc\"><span class=\"T286Pc\">Janis Provisor</span><span class=\"T286Pc\"> and <span class=\"T286Pc\">Brad Davis</span></span></span></strong> American artists who designed rugs for the Hermès home-decor line.</span></li>\n	<li><span class=\"T286Pc\"><strong class=\"Yjhzub\"><span class=\"T286Pc\"><span class=\"T286Pc\">Jean-Michel Franck</span></span></strong> A historical designer whose furnishings have been re-edited by Hermès.</span><span class=\"uJ19be notranslate\"><span class=\"vKEkVd\"> </span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<ul class=\"KsbFXc U6u95\">\n	<li> </li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"Y3BBE\">These individuals represent some of the creative talents whose work is preserved and referenced in the Hermès archives.<span class=\"uJ19be notranslate\"><span class=\"vKEkVd\"> </span></span></div>', '', '', ''),
